# Secrets. This file exists before .env does, deliberately - a key committed
# once is a key that lives in the history until the repo is rewritten.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Virtualenv
.venv/
venv/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Cached model replies. Regenerated by re-running the evaluation, and large
# enough to bloat the history - but note that deleting them costs real time
# (and, on a metered provider, real money) to rebuild.
data/cache/

# data/runs/ is NOT ignored, and used to be.
#
# It was grouped with the cache above under "regenerated by re-running", which
# is true of a cache and false of a result. A run file carries prompt_hash,
# golden_hash and model - it is the record of a measurement, and the whole
# argument for re-running it assumes the measurement is reproducible. For an
# evaluation whose scorer is deterministic that holds; for anything involving a
# model at temperature it does not, and "just re-run it" quietly means "get a
# different number and hope nobody diffs".
#
# 500K for ten runs. Cheaper than a figure nobody can check.

# Downloaded model weights, if any ever land here. GGUF files are gigabytes.
*.gguf
models/
